==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|es}} [[calabaza]] "[[pumpkin]], gourd", possibly from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|قرعة يابسة|sc=Arab|tr=qárʕa yābisa||dry gourd}} or directly from Persian ''(kharabuz)'' (denoting various large [[melon]]s), or from a pre-Roman Iberian word *[[calapaccia]]; cognate with French [[calebasse]] "[[gourd]]"

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|es}}

# A [[vine]] grown for its [[fruit]], which can either be harvested young and used as a vegetable or harvested mature, dried and used as a container, like a [[gourd]].
# (''originally'') That fruit
# A utensil traditionally made of the dried [[shell]] of a calabash and used as a bottle, dipper, utensil or pipe, etc.

